course: dictionary
lesson: 1302
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word cab is a good example.
explain: «People take a cab or call a cab to get across town.» The clues are take, call and across town, so cab means a taxi. But in «Toad eagerly scrambled up into the cab of the engine», the clue is the engine, so cab means the place where the driver sits.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Toad scrambled up into the taxi of the engine» does not make sense, so the driver's place is the right meaning. Check that your meaning fits the whole sentence.
fact: Cab means a taxi, a car with a driver you pay to take you somewhere.
fact: Cab also means the part of a lorry, truck, train or crane where the driver sits.
fact: «Take a cab», «call a cab» and «hail a cab» are all ways of getting a taxi.
fact: «Black cab» is a London taxi.
fact: «In the cab the driver controls the speed with a lever and watches the signals.»
exercise: «She waved down a cab outside the station.» What is a cab here? | A kind of railway track | *A taxi, a car with a driver you pay | The part of a crane where the driver sits | A sign at a bus stop
exercise: «Toad eagerly scrambled up into the cab of the engine.» What is the cab? | The wheels of the engine | *The place where the driver sits | The carriage for passengers | A taxi waiting outside
exercise: Ella says, «The lorry's cab was cold.» What does cab mean here? | A lorry driver's lunch box | A bus shelter | A taxi car | *The part of the lorry where the driver sits
test: «The train rattles off with Toad in the engine's cab.» Which clue tells you cab means the driver's place? | *engine's | rattles | fields | supper
test: Which phrase means to ask for a taxi to come to you? | the cab of a lorry | cab fares for maths | *call a cab | the cab of a crane
exam: «A truck driver cannot see a cyclist right beside the cab.» What does cab mean here? | *The place where the truck driver sits | A small room for passengers | A taxi you can call | The back of the truck
